    "q-79264": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79264",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14164726/assets/dfcaa1de127881d7f6291efa2f78fbaecf1e5e29cea00d6b071c6ed2b800026f.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $g$ defined by the mapping diagram shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $g(x)$ consists of all the outputs that have a corresponding $x$-input.\n\nIn a mapping diagram, the range consists of all the outputs to which an arrow is drawn.\n\nTherefore, the range is the set $\\{-\\frac{5}{2},0,2,6\\}.$",
